            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for poor, then the Marathi for dirt; dirty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: स्वच्छ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्वच्छ — svachchha — \"clean\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्वच्छ (svachchha) is Sanskrit svaccha, \"very clear, transparent\", taken over whole as a learned loan, a tatsama. It is su-, \"well\", and accha, \"clear\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
